Clear the update flags before the device thread starts

The device thread cleared CallFlag_UpdateLEDs and CallFlag_UpdateMode as
its first action. An UpdateLEDs() or UpdateMode() issued right after the
controller was constructed could set a flag before the thread got that
far, and the thread then cleared it, so the first update was lost.
Clearing the flags in the constructor, before the thread exists, closes
that window.

--- a/RGBController/RGBController.cpp
+++ b/RGBController/RGBController.cpp
@@ -100,2 +100,4 @@
     DeviceThreadRunning = true;
+    CallFlag_UpdateLEDs = false;
+    CallFlag_UpdateMode = false;
     DeviceCallThread    = new std::thread(&RGBController::DeviceCallThreadFunction, this);
@@ -2083,5 +2085,2 @@
 {
-    CallFlag_UpdateLEDs = false;
-    CallFlag_UpdateMode = false;
-
     while(DeviceThreadRunning.load() == true)
